meta {
  name: Refresh Truck RC (Surepass)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/trucks/{{rcTruckId}}/refresh-rc
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{vahnAdminToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.statusCode: eq 200
  res.body.data.id: eq {{rcTruckId}}
  res.body.data.registrationNumber: isString
}

docs {
  `TruckResource.refreshTruckRc`, VAHN_ADMIN only. Re-runs external RC verification
  (`TruckVerificationService.verifyTruckExternal`) for the truck and returns the updated TruckDTO
  wrapped by the response filter as `{data, message, statusCode, success}`. Bills a Surepass call and rewrites the truck's RC fields,
  so use a throwaway truck (staging: truck 1100, TN66AS6226) and set `rcTruckId` to it.

  If the truck is already VERIFIED / PAN_CARD_NOT_VALID / PAN_CARD_PENDING the service returns it
  as-is without calling Surepass (on staging truck 1100 was RC_NOT_VALID when checked 2026-10-21, so each call does bill Surepass).

  Other outcomes: unknown truck -> 404 `{"error":"Truck not found"}`; any other failure -> 500
  `{"error":"Failed to refresh RC details"}`. ENG-1309 outage branch (not reproducible on
  staging): Surepass 5xx after retries -> HTTP 503 `{"error": "<message>"}`, truck left PENDING and queued
  for background re-verification.

  Needs `{{vahnAdminToken}}`; pass it at run time with --env-var, never commit it.
}
